    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "The dual-frequency approach seems like the only way to prevent total identity erasure. I'll begin logging the amplitude of the isolated rhythmic impulses now.\n\nTo ensure the Order's archives can properly categorize these findings, we need a formal classification for these specific echo-signatures. If they represent the intersection of 19th-century prosody and 21st-century neuro-dynamics, how should we technically define this phenomenon in the stabilization report? I'm thinking of something like 'trans-temporal prosodic resonance'—does that align with the mathematical properties of the dual-frequency resonance you've just proposed?",
